          %title
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+spaces"} graded vector spaces
            equipped with
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Stasheff92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential graded Lie algebras, quasi-Hopf algebras and higher homotopy algebras
                %em Quantum groups
                Number 1510 in Lecture Notes in Math. Springer, Berlin, 1992 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0101184"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0101184
                ).
            %li#LadaStasheff92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Lada"}> Tom Lada
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to sh Lie algebras for physicists
                %strong 32
                (1993) 1087-1103 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00671791"}> doi:10.1007/BF00671791
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9209099"} arXiv:hep-th/9209099
            %li#LadaMarkl94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Lada"}> Tom Lada
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Markl"} Martin Markl
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Strongly homotopy Lie algebras
                %strong 23
                6 (1995) [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1080/00927879508825335"}> doi:10.1080/00927879508825335
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9406095"} arXiv:hep-th/9406095
            %li#Kontsevich97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                , Section 4.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Deformation quantization of Poisson manifolds, I
                %strong 66
                (2003) 157-216 (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9709040"}> arXiv:q-alg/9709040
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/B:MATH.0000027508.00421.bf"} doi:10.1023/B:MATH.0000027508.00421.bf
          %p
            At least
            %a{:href => "#Stasheff92"} Stasheff 92
            was following
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Zwiebach92"} Zwiebach 92
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+functions"} n-point functions
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+string+field+theory"} closed string field theory
            equip the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+string"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
            with
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "string+field+theory#ReferencesHomotopyAlgebra"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-formalism"} BV-formalism
            due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BatalinVilkovisky83"} Batalin-Vilkovisky 83
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BatakinFradkin83"} Batakin-Fradkin 83
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "L-infinity-algebra#History"} L-infinity algebra – History
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolutions"} cofibrant resolutions
            of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+operad"} Lie operad
          %ul
            %li#KrizMay95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"}> Igor Kriz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Operads, algebras, modules and motives
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 233
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/PAPERS/kmbooklatex.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=AST_1995__233__1_0"} numdam:AST_1995__233__1_0
            %li#LodayVallette12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Louis+Loday"}> Jean-Louis Loday
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruno+Vallette"} Bruno Vallette
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Operads
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 346
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9783642303616"} ISBN 978-3-642-30362-3
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://irma.math.unistra.fr/~loday/PAPERS/LodayVallette.pdf"} pdf
          %p A historical survey is
          %ul
            %li#Stasheff16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher homotopy structures, then and now
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/node/6356"} Opening workshop
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/node/5883"} Higher Structures in Geometry and Physics
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/StasheffHomotopyStructuresReview.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02526"} arXiv:1809.02526
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#Daily04
              %p
                Marilyn Daily,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                    \-structures
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.lib.ncsu.edu/resolver/1840.16/5282"} web
            %li
              %p
                Klaus Bering,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Lada"} Tom Lada
                %em Examples of Homotopy Lie Algebras
                Archivum Mathematicum (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0903.5433"}> arXiv:0903.5433
                )
          %p
            Comprehensive survey with emphasis on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra+cohomology"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-algebra cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              Ben Reinhold,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                  \-algebras and their cohomology
              %strong 3
              4 (2019) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1051/emsci/2019003"}> doi:10.1051/emsci/2019003
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Review for the special case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebras"} Lie 2-algebras
            with emphasis on the perspective of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alissa+Crans"} Alissa Crans
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher-dimensional algebra VI: Lie 2-algebras
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/12/14/12-14abs.html"} TAC
              12, (2004), 492–528. (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0307263"}> arXiv:math/0307263
              )
          %h3#as_models_for_rational_homotopy_types As models for rational homotopy types
          %p
            That
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            is implicit in
            %a{:href => "rational+homotopy+theory#Quillen69"} Quillen 69
            (via their
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+dg-Lie+algebras#RectificationResolution"} equivalence with dg-Lie algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Hinich98"} Hinich 98
          %ul
